# Coding Style

- Match the conventions already used in the surrounding file; do not
  introduce a new style in an existing module.
- No unused imports, no dead code, no commented-out blocks left in commits.
- Every function that is part of a public API (route, exported function,
  component) needs a docstring/JSDoc explaining purpose, params, return.
- Prefer explicit names over abbreviations.
- Add/extend tests for any new logic branch (see `tester` agent).
- Run the project's linter/formatter before considering a task complete.
- Keep functions under ~50 lines where reasonably possible; extract helpers
  otherwise.

## Persian comments / docs (required)
- Write **docstrings / JSDoc and explanatory comments in Persian (فارسی)**.
- Comment **only where it helps**: public functions, non-obvious business
  rules, workarounds, invariants, and tricky edge cases.
- Do **not** comment every line. Do not narrate obvious code
  (`i++ // افزایش شمارنده` is banned).
- Prefer a short Persian docstring on the function over five inline
  comments inside it.
- Keep identifiers (function/variable/class names) in English per the
  project's naming rules; only human-facing explanations are Persian.
- Commit messages and PR/MR titles stay in Conventional Commits English
  unless the human explicitly asks otherwise.
